# line 358: NET_C(FOLLA.GND, FOLLA.IC_8B.4, FOLLA.IC_C8.5, FOLLA.IC_7B.8, FOLLA.IC_8B.10, FOLLA.IC_8B.13, FOLLA.IC_C8.10, FOLLA.IC_E8.4) -> nc -- as line 357
# line 357: MAME ties UB7.12, UB7.10, UB7.2, UB7.8 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
# line 358: MAME ties UB7.8 off as unused, but the circuit uses them -- the tie is dropped
#
# Corrected from the MEF00284 board schematic, sound section (manual PDF p. 11):
#   UD7: the sheet's part is 74LS161, MAME's 74161 -- printed LS161; MAME's 74161 has its pins
#   UE7: the sheet's part is 74LS161, MAME's 74161 -- printed LS161; MAME's 74161 has its pins
#   UL9: the sheet's part is 7404, MAME's 7414 -- printed '04 beside L9's gate on the AD4 line; MAME's generic inverter sub-netlist is a 7414
#   CALCIO_A_C30: the sheet's value is 47nF, MAME's 68nF -- printed '47K' (nF), and MAME's line 541 says 47 -- meant for CAP2, it sets CAP1 again
#   CALCIO_A_C33: the sheet's value is 22nF, MAME's 47nF -- printed '22K' (nF), as MAME's line 540 sets it before line 541 overrides it
#   CALCIO_A_C34: the sheet's value is 22nF, MAME's 47nF -- as C33
#   CALCIO_B_C33: the sheet's value is 33nF, MAME's 68nF -- printed '33K' (nF), as MAME's line 544 sets it before line 545 overrides it with the 68 meant for CAP2
#   CALCIO_B_C34: the sheet's value is 33nF, MAME's 68nF -- as C33
#   R_FISCHIO: the sheet's value is 100K, MAME's 220K -- printed 100K where the whistle enters the mix
#   R_PARATA: the sheet's value is 47K, MAME's 100K -- printed 47K where the save sound enters the mix (the drafter crosses a 7, and it reads like a 2: '42K')
#   parts the sheet draws that MAME does not have: VRA 2.2K, VRB 2.2K, VRC 47K, PARATA_Q3 2N3819, PARATA_RS 1K
#   kick A's 68K, 220K and 10K to +12, as printed: CALCIO_A_R52.2 CALCIO_A_R48.2 CALCIO_A_R55.2
#   kick B's to +12 -- its arrows carry no label, and B is A's circuit drawn the same way: CALCIO_B_R52.2 CALCIO_B_R48.2 CALCIO_B_R55.2
#   VR-A from kick A's first transistor's emitter to ground, its wiper to ground: CALCIO_A_Q8.E VRA.1; VRA.2 VRA.3
#   VR-B from kick B's first transistor's emitter to ground, its wiper to ground: CALCIO_B_Q8.E VRB.1; VRB.2 VRB.3
#   the second JFET's source, the save's output, to ground through 1K: PARATA_Q3.S PARATA_RS.1; PARATA_RS.2
#   the mix to VR-C's top, its bottom to ground: Q_OUT.C VRC.1 (MIX); VRC.3
#   VR-C's wiper, through 10uF/16V to the TDA2003's pin 1: VRC.2 (AMP_IN)
#   B7 pin 9 is driven by 32H, where MAME runs an ideal 40 kHz clock: UB7.9 (32H)
#   B7's first gate inverts /RESET into RES, the 8255s' reset: UB7.1 (RESETQ); UB7.2 (RES)
#   L9 gates AD3 (in on 3, out on 4) and AD4 (5 to 6) into the 8255s' chip selects: UL9.3 (AD3); UL9.4 (AD3Q); UL9.5 (AD4); UL9.6 (AD4Q)
# line 153: CALCIO_A.R0 is not a part, and its two ends are one node here -- a 1 ohm resistor MAME adds at the sub-circuit's output so that its solver can split the netlist there (OPTIMIZE_FRONTIER)
# line 153: CALCIO_B.R0 is not a part, and its two ends are one node here -- a 1 ohm resistor MAME adds at the sub-circuit's output so that its solver can split the netlist there (OPTIMIZE_FRONTIER)
# line 188: STOP_PALLA.R0 is not a part, and its two ends are one node here -- a 1 ohm resistor MAME adds at the sub-circuit's output so that its solver can split the netlist there (OPTIMIZE_FRONTIER)
# line 209: PARATA.D2 is not a part -- a diode across the first 2N3819's gate and source, which the sheet ties together -- MAME's model of the JFET's gate junction (it models a JFET as a MOSFET, which has none); not on the sheet
# line 210: PARATA.D3 is not a part -- a diode from the second 2N3819's gate to its source -- MAME's model of the JFET's gate junction; not on the sheet
# line 344: FISCHIO.R0 is not a part, and its two ends are one node here -- a 1 ohm resistor MAME adds at the sub-circuit's output so that its solver can split the netlist there (OPTIMIZE_FRONTIER)
# line 427: FOLLA.R0 is not a part, and its two ends are one node here -- a 1 ohm resistor MAME adds at the sub-circuit's output so that its solver can split the netlist there (OPTIMIZE_FRONTIER)
# line 618: OUTPUT_FILTER is not a part -- MAME's own third-order Sallen-Key low-pass (an op-amp on +-12V, three resistors, three capacitors), added 'to avoid aliasing when outputing at 48KHz', its file says; on the board the mix goes to the volume pot VR-C and the TDA2003 amplifier
# MAME declares one section of these packages at a time; each is written on its package's
# pins by the data sheet's numbering of the sections (SECTION_PINS in the converter): UB7 7414 (INV1.IC_L9, INV2.IC_L9, INV3.IC_L9); UB9 LM339 (PARATA.IC_B9, STOP_PALLA.IC_B9); UL9 7404 (FISCHIO.INV.IC_L9)
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): TTL_INPUT(I_PB0), TTL_INPUT(I_PB1), TTL_INPUT(I_PB2), TTL_INPUT(I_PB3), TTL_INPUT(I_PB4), TTL_INPUT(I_PB5), TTL_INPUT(I_PB6), TTL_INPUT(I_PB7), CLOCK(clk), TTL_INPUT(I_FISCHIO), TTL_INPUT(I_STOP_PALLA), TTL_INPUT(I_PARATA), TTL_INPUT(I_CALCIO_A), TTL_INPUT(I_CALCIO_B), TTL_INPUT(I_FOLLA_A), TTL_INPUT(I_FOLLA_M), TTL_INPUT(I_FOLLA_B), TTL_INPUT(I_CONTRASTO), TTL_INPUT(ENABLE_SOUND)
# Lines 121, 141 and 142 (in calcio, so in both kicks) are taken out whole: R54, 'WAS POT',
# is the trimmer VR-A or VR-B, put back from the sheet below. Lines 292-296 (in the inverter
# sub-netlist, so in all four instances) tie the 7414's outputs 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12 to ground;
# here each instance is one gate of a package the sheet names, so the lines go.
#
# Compared with the sound section of the MEF00284 schematic (the Dribbling service manual,
# doc 64210d7094ce, PDF p. 11, a 1-bit scan at about 370 dpi), on 2026-10-20 -- every
# sub-circuit, net by net, and every value printed. MAME's topology agrees with the sheet
# everywhere: the TOS divider (E7 and D7 loaded from PB4-PB7 and PB0-PB3, E7's carry to
# both loads through B7 and to C7's J and K, C7 pin 5 the output), the crowd's noise
# generator (A8 and A7 with B8's XOR feedback, clocked by B7's RC oscillator) and its three
# gated levels into the LM324 band-pass at C8, the 556 'contrasto' at Q9, the whistle's 556
# at N9 counted by M9 (MAME's 100K and 47K both end on N9's 12/8 node, as drawn), the two
# comparators of B9, and the mix (ENABLE_SOUND through 2.2K to a BC239 that shorts the mix to
# ground). The ICs agree in type and pin number wherever the sheet prints them: B9 pins 5,
# 4, 2 for the stop and 11, 10, 13 for the save; N9 and Q9 pin for pin; M9's 2 and 12, 1,
# 6 and 13.
#
# Corrected above from the sheet: kick A's supply resistors go to +12 (B's arrows are
# unlabelled, and taken as A's); the trimmers VR-A and VR-B are pots wired as rheostats,
# not MAME's 1.9K; the kicks' twin-T capacitors are the sheet's (MAME's file says what it
# meant -- 22, 47 for A and 33, 68 for B -- but its PARAM lines set CAP1 twice, so it runs
# A with 47nF, 47nF, 68nF and B with 68nF all round); the whistle enters the mix through
# 100K, not 220K, and the save through 47K, not 100K; the save's output has a 1K source
# resistor; and the mix goes to the volume pot VR-C, where MAME has a filter of its own.
# D7 and E7 are printed LS161 and L9 '04. MAME's four inverters are gates of the sheet's
# packages, by its pin numbers: TOS's load gate is B7 11 to 10 (the sheet prints 11 at the
# output), its clock gate 13 to 12, the 32H gate 9 to 8, and the whistle's reset gate L9
# 13 to 12 (printed 13 and 9).
#
# Open, and kept as MAME has them: the drafter's crossed 7 reads like a 2, and five
# capacitors print as '4,2uF' -- each kick's from collector to twin-T (MAME 4.2uF) and its
# emitter capacitor (MAME 4.7uF), and the whistle's timing capacitor (MAME 4.2uF). 4.2uF is
# not a standard value and MAME itself reads two of them as 4.7uF, so all five are probably
# 4.7uF; the print does not show it. The stop's series resistor prints 1?0K, the middle
# digit unclear (MAME 160K; the save's is 150K). The dashed, so optional, pull-up on ABIL.
# AMPLIFICATORE reads 1?K; MAME's is 10K. The unlabelled supply arrows (the 556s' timing
# resistors, the BC309 emitters, the comparators' 2.2K pull-ups, the second JFET's drain,
# the crowd filter's bias) are taken as +5V, as MAME has them; only the kicks are marked
# +12. Which terminal of each JFET is source and which drain the drawing does not say;
# MAME's choice fits the topology. The diodes are printed BAX (a Philips switching diode),
# for which MAME's 1N914 is a like part. E7's and D7's clears, D7's enables and the
# counters' supply pins are not drawn; MAME's ties are kept.
#
# On the sheet and not in this file: the TDA2003 at the output (10uF in, 220 ohm and 2.2
# ohm feedback with 470uF, 1000uF out to the 8 ohm speaker on edge pins 16 and 17, a 0.1uF
# and 1 ohm Zobel) and its '+12Vcc M.S.' decoupling; the supplies -- a 26MB bridge into
# 22,000uF, a 323 for +5V with 6.8 ohms 10W across it, an LM320 for -5V, and a 7812
# (printed 2812) beside an unregulated +12V through two 1N4004s, so which +12V the kicks'
# '+12' is the sheet does not say; and the two 8255s, at K8 and below it, whose port bits
# the ports here are.

